/* Design grid: 19.2 × 10.8 rem (1920 × 1080 at 1 rem = 100 px). The scale is the viewport fit ("contain").
   1 rem floor: the old 40 px was a phone guess and it backfired on short landscape screens — the design is 432 px
   tall at 40 px, so on a 390–440 px tall phone the chrome kept its desktop size while the board was squeezed into the
   leftover ~42 %; the floor is now only as large as the chrome needs to stay usable, and the fit formula decides.
   2 rem ceiling: 4K and ultrawide keep their 1 rem = 100 px design size instead of scaling forever. */
font-size: clamp(20px, min(calc(100vw / 19.2), calc(100vh / 10.8)) * var(--sp-font-scale, 1), 240px);

/* Short landscape phones (≤ 460 CSS px tall): the board is what the player watches, so the HUD strip and the shop bar
   give up their extra padding and the shop cards lose a little size — every touch target keeps a pixel floor (the
   confirm strip stays ≥ 34 px, a card stays ≥ 54 px wide), and the rem scale already fits the design into the screen
   (css/theme.css). Before this the chrome took 57–59 % of a 390 px tall screen and left the board 42 %. */
@media (max-height: 460px) {
  .gtop { padding: .1rem .2rem 0 .18rem; gap: .14rem; }
  .gm__bonds { top: 1.24rem; }
  .team { top: 2.2rem; gap: .1rem; }
  .shopbar { bottom: .08rem; gap: .06rem; }
  .shopbar__row { padding: .06rem; gap: .06rem; }
  .shopbar__cards, .shopbar__item { gap: .06rem; }
  .scard { width: 1.4rem; height: 1.98rem; }
  .lvcard { height: 2rem; }
  .gm__corner { bottom: .08rem; }
}

